{"created": "2025-09-11T08:21:46.480410+00:00", "modified": "2025-10-22T20:02:46.121419+00:00", "id": 17086687, "conceptrecid": "17086686", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17086687", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.17086686", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17086687", "metadata": {"title": "Low cycle fatigue data of wrought and additively manufactured stainless steels for constiutive model development", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17086687", "publication_date": "2025-09-09", "description": "<p>This dataset provides the underlying data for a full numerical verification for a revised Chaboche constitutive model for a variety of stainless steels. This dataset includes multiple strain amplitudes from initial loading to saturation and final rupture (&Delta;&epsilon; = 0.4%&ndash;1.0%). Also included are example fitting of Chaboche parameters in an accompanying document.</p>\n<p>Contents:</p>\n<p>- Compressed archive of *.csv files collected from an INSTRON 8800MT servo-hydraulic machine controlled by WaveMatrix3 software. Strain measurements were recorded using a 2632 Series axial extensometer. Data, including cycle number, strain, time, force, and actuator position were collected continuously at a sampling frequency of 10 Hz. Test specimens were machined into double-ended threaded rods with a central reduced gauge section according to ASTM E606-04. All column headings reflect quantities recorded, file prefixes reflect material and strain amplitude for each test.</p>\n<p>Prefixes of A, B and C reflect as-received wrought 316L, normalised wrought 316L and as-received wrought 304 stainless steels respectively. H and V reflect as-received laser powder bed fusion (L-PBF) samples, where H is an orientation orthogonal to the substrate, and V is parallel.</p>\n<p>The 'Verfification.pdf' contains exemplar constitutive Chaboche parameters for each of the included tests.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Huo, Runxin", "affiliation": "Henry Royce Institute", "orcid": 